  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run, with all 9 witnesses passing; 5 runs of the budget are left. I made no narrowings because the node left no reading open, and I found nothing wrong with the node.\n\n**The rule** (`LVMC_11_20_060_o3.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be in the vehicle aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **When it applies:** the business-or-residence-district assumption holds, and the subject is emerging onto a roadway. That means it occupies a roadway region and a driveway/alley-entrance or alley region at once. It must also have stayed on that driveway or alley at every observation since one where it was on the driveway or alley and not the roadway. Because a region quantifier takes only one kind, the driveway and alley cases are written as two quantifiers joined by \"or\".\n- **What it requires:** the obligation selects the roadway again with the same formula. Then, for every other vehicle on that roadway, both of these must hold:\n  - the subject is not moving faster than `p.halt_speed_tolerance` while the constant-velocity closest approach within `p.conflict_horizon` comes closer than `p.conflict_centre_clearance`;\n  - the subject is not in contact with that vehicle.\n\n**The witnesses:** the five the node plans (forbid, permit, idle, blind with `rel.occupies` masked, and branch_1) plus four I added so every part of the formula changes some witness's verdict:\n\n| Witness | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| branch_2 | The subject halts touching a car standing on the roadway, so only the contact check catches it | violated |\n| branch_3 | The subject emerges from an alley instead of a driveway | violated |\n| branch_4 | The road user crossing in front is a pedestrian, not a vehicle | compliant |\n| branch_5 | The car is on the other roadway of a divided highway | compliant |\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
